-- title:
--   Newform behind a geometric point of the local Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho\colon \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})\to\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, and assume its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $N\neq 0$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ spanned over $\mathbb C$ by the lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Finally let $\chi$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the localised Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisation of the base-changed algebra at the complement of the prime kernel of $\theta$) to an algebraic closure of $\mathrm{Frac}\,\mathcal O$. Then there are a level $M_g\neq 0$ dividing $N$, a cusp form $g$ of weight two on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose good eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of $M_g$), a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from the full Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M_g$ and $\chi_g(U_q)=a_q(g)$ for all primes $q\mid M_g$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\overline{\mathrm{Frac}\,\mathcal O}$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ one has $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\chi(\pi(T_\ell))$, where $\pi$ is the structure map from the anemic Hecke algebra of level $N$ to its localisation.
--
--   This identifies the newform attached to a geometric point of the localised anemic Hecke algebra, with the accompanying eigencharacter taken on the full Hecke algebra of level $M_g$ so that the coefficients $a_q(g)$ at primes $q\in S$ with $q\nmid M_g$ are also available in $\overline{\mathrm{Frac}\,\mathcal O}$. It feeds the computations of newform multiplicities and of sums of root multiplicities in the localised Hecke algebra used in the level-lowering argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeLocal_exists_isNewform_chig_full_iota_of_algHom_algebraicClosure.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeLocal
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_Newforms
import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_LocalConditions
import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_Residual
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.AlgebraicClosure
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.FractionRing

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
